    {
      "id": "p0018-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Every language has its own unique rules and quirks. Every culture has its own unique values and expectations. Because of this, not every word has a perfect, 1-to-l equivalent in other languages. So when a straightforward, literal translation isn't possible, one alternative is to use completely different words to say the same thing. And that's precisely what localization is: preserving the creator's intended meaning but with completely different words. As the acclaimed translator John Ciardi once put it:",
        "raw": "Every language has its own unique rules and quirks. Every culture has its\nown unique values and expectations. Because of this, not every word has a\nperfect, 1-to-l equivalent in other languages. So when a straightforward, literal\ntranslation isn't possible, one alternative is to use completely different words\nto say the same thing. And that's precisely what localization is: preserving the\ncreator's intended meaning but with completely different words. As the\nacclaimed translator John Ciardi once put it:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29040798,
          0.09132857,
          0.89460833,
          0.21407857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28887207,
          0.09061429,
          0.89713087,
          0.21550714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "每种语言都有自己的规则和特点，每种文化也有自己的价值观和预期。因此，并不是每个词都能在另一种语言中找到一一对应的词。无法直接照字面翻译时，一种办法就是换一套完全不同的说法，表达同样的意思。这正是本地化：用完全不同的词，保留创作者想表达的意思。正如著名译者 John Ciardi 所说：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29090638,
          0.09,
          0.89713087,
          0.40357143
        ],
