    {
      "id": "p0018-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In short, languages are weird, messy, and complicated. It's easy for people to misunderstand each other in one language, so translating between two can sometimes be impossible. In this chapter, we'll examine a few situations in which straightforward, literal translations don't quite work.",
        "raw": "In short, languages are weird, messy, and complicated. It's easy for people to\nmisunderstand each other in one language, so translating between two can\nsometimes be impossible. In this chapter, we'll examine a few situations in\nwhich straightforward, literal translations don't quite work.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29048935,
          0.32967143,
          0.87489586,
          0.39621429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28887207,
          0.32895714,
          0.89713087,
          0.39764286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "总之，语言古怪、杂乱而复杂。用同一种语言，人们都容易误解彼此；在两种语言之间翻译，有时甚至是不可能的任务。本章将介绍一些直接照字面翻译不太行得通的情形。",
