    {
      "id": "p0018-b015",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "So, as a translator, what do you do when you run into an untranslatable joke? The most common solution is to take out the original joke and replace it with a similar joke that works in the target language. And that's precisely what localization is all about: retaining the original intent even if it means changing the original words.",
        "raw": "So, as a translator, what do you do when you run into an untranslatable joke?\nThe most common solution is to take out the original joke and replace it with\na similar joke that works in the target language. And that's precisely what\nlocalization is all about: retaining the original intent even if it means changing\nthe original words.",
        "status": "corrected",
